Lithium has atomic number \(Z=3\). If nucleus \(X\) has 3 neutrons, then it is lithium-6:

\[
A = Z + N = 3 + 3 = 6
\]

For speed \(v = 0.96c\),

\[
\gamma = \frac{1}{\sqrt{1-\beta^2}}
= \frac{1}{\sqrt{1-0.96^2}}
= \frac{1}{\sqrt{0.0784}}
= 3.5714286
\]

Using the tabulated atomic mass of \(^6\text{Li}\),

\[
m(^6\text{Li}) \approx 6.015122\ \text{u}
\]

and

\[
1\ \text{u}c^2 \approx 931.494\ \text{MeV}
\]

the rest energy is

\[
E_0 = 6.015122 \times 931.494\ \text{MeV}
\approx 5603.05\ \text{MeV}
= 5.60305\ \text{GeV}
\]

The total relativistic energy is

\[
E = \gamma E_0
\approx 3.5714286 \times 5.60305\ \text{GeV}
\approx 20.0109\ \text{GeV}
\]

Rounded to the required precision:

\[
E \approx 20.011\ \text{GeV}
\]

Answer: A
